Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission, P2E): preserve surface metadata
across merged-region perimeter generation in `Layer::make_perimeters`.

Ported from FS v0.9.9 (`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit
b3c41fda), `src/libslic3r/Layer.cpp` +49 LoC.

Why this matters even before Local-Z lands:

When multiple compatible regions share perimeter parameters (same wall
count, same line widths, same flow ratios), `Layer::make_perimeters`
merges their slices into one set for a single PerimeterGenerator pass.
The prior code grouped surfaces solely by `extra_perimeters` count,
which collapsed surfaces with the same extra_perimeters but different
thickness / bridge_angle / thickness_layers into one group; downstream
the merged set lost those fields. Bridge angle in particular dropped to
zero on merged-region surfaces, which then printed as flat infill
instead of angled bridge spans.

The prior re-split path (assigning fill_surfaces back to originating
regions after perimeter generation) also lost per-surface-type
information — used a single `intersection_ex` over fill_surfaces,
which preserves only the surface type of `fill_surfaces.surfaces.front()`
on the merged output.

This patch:

1. Adds `SliceMergeKey` tuple (type, thickness, thickness_layers,
   bridge_angle, extra_perimeters) and `slice_merge_key()` helper that
   groups surfaces by every load-bearing trait.

2. Adds `split_fill_surfaces_by_region` helper that iterates each
   `SurfaceType` and clips fill_surfaces of that type against the
   per-region slices, preserving type assignment in the output.

3. `Layer::make_perimeters` switches both group-merge and re-split
   paths to the new helpers, with `ApplySafetyOffset::Yes` on the
   `fill_no_overlap_expolygons` intersection to match FS shape.

Verified compile-clean via incremental libslic3r rebuild (37/37 objects,
0 FAILED) + ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug (full APK assembled).

Ships independently of any FS mixed-filament feature — pure quality
improvement to merged-region perimeter generation. Companion to:
  - 0029 (ExtrusionEntity inset_idx propagation)
  - 0030 (PerimeterGenerator inset_idx population)
  - 0031 (VariableWidth gap-fill loop dedup)
  - 0032 (LayerRegion virtual filament resolution)

